---
import Layout from '../layouts/Layout.astro';
import SectionHeader from '../components/SectionHeader.astro';
---

<Layout title="AI - takmd" description="AI integration in clinical spine surgery practice.">
  <section class="page-shell py-14">
    <h1 class="page-title-gradient text-4xl font-extrabold sm:text-5xl">AI Integration in Clinical Spine Practice</h1>
    <p class="mt-4 text-base text-[var(--color-link)]">AI assists cognition, not replaces surgeons.</p>
  </section>

  <section class="page-shell space-y-8 pb-16">
    <div>
      <SectionHeader icon="🧠" title="Workflow Augmentation" />
      <p class="max-w-3xl text-[var(--color-text-secondary)]">
        AI supports preoperative and postoperative workflow continuity by reducing repetitive synthesis tasks and helping
        maintain structured clinical context across encounters.
      </p>
    </div>

    <div>
      <SectionHeader icon="🗂️" title="Documentation Assist" />
      <p class="max-w-3xl text-[var(--color-text-secondary)]">
        Voice-to-structured note pipelines reduce documentation burden while preserving surgeon review at every stage of
        final clinical communication.
      </p>
    </div>

    <div>
      <SectionHeader icon="📊" title="Registry Structuring" />
      <p class="max-w-3xl text-[var(--color-text-secondary)]">
        Standardized fields and consistent tagging support prospective data quality and simplify later analysis for quality
        improvement and publication-ready registries.
      </p>
    </div>

    <div>
      <SectionHeader icon="✅" title="Decision Checklist Support" />
      <p class="max-w-3xl text-[var(--color-text-secondary)]">
        Prompt-driven checklists offer cognitive safety rails around indications, contraindications, and expected outcomes,
        while final decisions remain physician-led.
      </p>
    </div>

    <a href="/ai-workflow" class="inline-flex text-sm font-medium text-[var(--color-link)] transition-colors hover:text-[var(--color-text)]">
      See the detailed workflow ->
    </a>
  </section>
</Layout>
